@startuml
title Sequence Diagram - Purchase Request Approval and PO Handoff

actor Requester
actor "Department Executive" as Executive
actor Manager
participant "React Purchasing Pages" as FE
participant "Workflow API" as WF
participant "Budget API" as Budget
participant "Notification Service" as NS
database "Prisma / PostgreSQL" as DB

Requester -> FE: Submit PR payload
FE -> FE: Validate required fields and totals
FE -> Budget: POST /usage/reserve
Budget -> DB: Check department budget
alt insufficient budget
  Budget --> FE: 409 insufficient budget
  FE --> Requester: Show budget error
else budget reserved
  FE -> WF: PUT /api/workflow/purchase-requests {rows}
  WF -> DB: Upsert status=SUBMITTED
  WF -> WF: Determine approver by role + department
  WF -> NS: Trigger submission notification
  NS -> DB: Save requester and approver alerts
  NS --> Executive: In-app + email (Employee request)
  NS --> Manager: In-app + email (Executive request)
end

alt Employee request
  Executive -> FE: Open request detail
else Department Executive request
  Manager -> FE: Open request detail
else Manager request
  Requester -> FE: Open self-approval detail
end

Executive -> FE: Approve / request change / reject
Manager -> FE: Approve / request change / reject
FE -> WF: PUT PR with decision and reason
WF -> DB: Save status and audit payload
alt REQUEST_CHANGE or REJECTED
  WF -> Budget: Release or recalculate reservation
  WF -> NS: Notify requester with comments/reason
else APPROVED
  WF -> DB: Create PO draft from approved PR
  WF -> NS: Notify requester of approval
end

Executive -> FE: Review and submit PO draft
FE -> WF: PUT /api/workflow/purchase-orders {status=PENDING_MANAGER}
WF -> DB: Persist PO and manager target
WF -> NS: Notify Manager
NS --> Manager: In-app + email approval alert
@enduml
